WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
I'm recording one second of every day&nbsp;
of my life for the rest of my life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.810
chronologically compiling 
these one-second

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.120
tiny&nbsp;slices of my life into 
one single continuous video

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.433
until, you know,

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:14.138
I can't record them anymore.

00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:17.185
The purpose of this project is, one:

00:00:17.185 --> 00:00:19.831
I hate not remembering things 
that I've done in the past.

00:00:19.831 --> 00:00:21.860
There's all these things 
that I've done with my life

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.935
that I have no recollection of 
unless&nbsp;someone brings it up,

00:00:24.935 --> 00:00:25.770
and sometimes I think,

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.865
"Oh yeah, that's something that I did."

00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:32.453
It's&nbsp;also kind of a personal protest, 
against the culture we have now

00:00:32.453 --> 00:00:35.620
where people&nbsp;just are at concerts 
with their cell phones out

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.872
recording the whole concert.

00:00:36.872 --> 00:00:39.354
I admittedly&nbsp;used to be that 
guy a little bit, back in the day,

00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:41.730
and I've decided that the best way

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.616
for me&nbsp;to still capture and keep

00:00:44.616 --> 00:00:47.157
a visual memory of my life

00:00:47.157 --> 00:00:48.408
and not be that person,

00:00:48.408 --> 00:00:49.820
is to just&nbsp;record that one second

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.175
that will allow me to 
trigger that memory of,

00:00:52.175 --> 00:00:55.388
"Yeah, that concert&nbsp;was amazing. 
I really loved that concert."

